A spec that changes the interface sets `ui: true` in its frontmatter, and must show
what the change looks like before it is done: screenshots in `{{ index .Caps "visual.evidence" }}/`,
linked from an `## Evidence` section, one per acceptance criterion that describes
something visible.

There are no baseline images and no pixel diffing. A person looks. Nothing can
automate whether a layout is right, and pretending otherwise produces a suite that
fails on every intentional change and gets ignored within a week.

"The component renders" is not evidence. A screenshot of the state a user will
actually be in is.
